# The free-energy file of D161 on a device where the particles are put in
# order, with a checkpoint every 10 steps and from the checkpoint of
# another state, against the CPU in double precision
# (Inputs/check_free_energy_reorder.py; issue #26).
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, hdf5
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_free_energy_reorder.py %t mdir MIXED | FileCheck %s
# RUN: mdir emit %t/ordered.toml --stage=module | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MAP
# RUN: rm -rf %t-double && mkdir -p %t-double
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_free_energy_reorder.py %t-double mdir DOUBLE | FileCheck %s
#
# CHECK: with checkpoints, finite: ok
# CHECK: with checkpoints, device against CPU: ok
# CHECK: with checkpoints, dH/dl against central differences: ok
# CHECK: same-state continuation, finite: ok
# CHECK: same-state continuation, device against CPU: ok
# CHECK: same-state continuation, dH/dl against central differences: ok
# CHECK: from another state, finite: ok
# CHECK: from another state, device against CPU: ok

# Verify that the step potential exercises the mapped-charge producer,
# rather than masking #26 with the former host-computed q_rec field.
# MAP-LABEL: md.potential @energy(
# MAP: %q_scaled = md.map_particles
# MAP: md.reciprocal %x, %q_scaled,
